{"summary":"Verified all five amendments against the current codebase, including a fresh cargo check for tank_data. Two amendments describe real gaps worth fixing: missing DO/alkalinity volume-independence assertions and loss of explicit zero/custom substrate area multipliers. Two are factually stale because the cited rename and algae-normalization issues are already fixed. One is technically redundant: the extreme-scale test omits the Monod block, but equivalent Monod-factor coverage already exists elsewhere, so it does not expose a real untested defect.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-008e032a","decision":"accept","rationale":"The volume-independence test records and compares only TAN, NO2, NO3, DOC, and DON deltas. It does not assert dissolved oxygen or alkalinity deltas, even though nitrogen_cycle updates both through budgeted total-mass bookkeeping that depends on volume. A volume-scaling bug in those DO/alkalinity paths would currently slip through this regression, so adding those assertions is a legitimate coverage fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-7e77d2a4","decision":"reject","rationale":"It is true that the 1 L vs 1000 L test does not repeat the Monod-factor block from the 10 L vs 100 L test, but the codebase already has separate Monod-factor coverage in per_guild_monod_uses_concentration_not_total across 1, 10, 100, and 1000 L, and the primary integration-style test already checks Monod factors plus per-liter deltas together. Adding the same block to the extreme-scale test would be redundant rather than closing a real correctness or robustness gap."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-0afb1776","decision":"reject","rationale":"The claimed build break is not present. cargo check -p tank_data succeeds, validation already references the renamed concentration-based fields, and the cited stale line is just TOML test data rather than Rust code accessing removed struct members. This amendment is based on an outdated reading of the file, not a current compile failure."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-e1c5d607","decision":"reject","rationale":"The parser already normalizes legacy algae half-saturation total-mass keys into the per-liter fields, and it also migrates the corresponding param_meta keys. Regression tests for both algae value migration and algae param_meta migration are already present. The described 20x loading bug is therefore not a current defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-905ce34d","decision":"accept","rationale":"This is a real data-integrity bug. resolved_colonizable_area_factor treats 0.0 as missing, refresh_habitat_registry writes that fallback back into state, substrate preset validation explicitly allows zero, and the v6 to v7 migration hard-codes kind defaults instead of preserving custom scaling encoded in saved area. As a result, an intentional zero or custom multiplier can be silently replaced. Preserving explicit zero/custom values is the correct fix direction."}]}